# halium.config reorders CONFIG_LSM to put apparmor ahead of selinux, which is
# what Ubuntu Touch needs: only one LSM_FLAG_EXCLUSIVE module initialises
# (prepare_lsm() in security/security.c skips the rest), so whichever comes
# first wins and the other is silently dead.
#
# This file used to undo that and make SELinux the exclusive one, because
# mayfly's stock /vendor/bin/vndservicemanager aborts without selinuxfs and
# nothing brought up the display. That cost AppArmor, and with it every click
# app: lomiri-app-launch runs them through aa-exec, which then always failed
# with "AppArmor interface not available".
#
# The real fix is upstream's: preload libselinux_stubs.so into
# vndservicemanager (see overlay/system/usr/share/halium-overlay/), so it no
# longer needs selinuxfs and AppArmor can stay. Nothing to override here any
# more -- keep the file so deviceinfo_kernel_defconfig does not have to change,
# and so the history of why is not lost.
